# automation-review-authorization-ci-boundary — History

## v2.2.0 (2026-08-03)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2157 / PR #2596 automation-loop review and merge.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Added a concrete iterative review example: NOGO → GO → NOGO → GO across successive exact heads.
- Documented that a later review finding retracts an earlier GO before merge-wait.
- Recorded the final reviewed head, loop-owned label transitions, independent required-check timing, and merge commit.

### Why

PR #2596 showed that the automation loop must treat each addressed review batch as a new
authorization attempt. Five initial findings were addressed before GO, but a later review
found a remaining `create_pr` title-normalization gap; the loop removed GO, applied NOGO,
and only restored GO after the final head was reviewed. Required checks then completed before
merge-wait merged that exact head, preserving the CI/review authorization boundary.

### Previous version (v2.1.0) snapshot

