## v2.1.0 (2026-08-03)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #1950 / PR #2590 automation-loop review and merge.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Added the direct-issue context invariant: hydrate the original issue title/body into the
  work-item payload before planning and carry it into initial/amended prompts with fencing.
- Added a completed-run audit for PR #2590 showing that only the final exact-head review
  authorized the GO transition; earlier review receipts stayed historical.
- Recorded that required checks completed after the GO label and before merge, independently
  of the loop-owned authorization.

### Why

PR #2590 fixed direct issue planning context while its review path crossed several heads. The
final head, not an earlier review receipt, was the only revision eligible for authorization.
The live event order also demonstrates that CI completion can remain a merge prerequisite
without becoming the source of review authorization.

