## v2.0.0 (2026-07-25)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2448 / PR #2449 direct-PR review and merge path.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Generalized the skill around metadata-only direct-PR admission and exact-head checkout-derived review evidence.
- Replaced the stale auto-merge-arm handoff with the current exact-reviewed-head merge-wait path; native auto-merge remains outside queue ownership.
- Added the transient live-GitHub-facts block/retry rule and clarified that review prose, grades, and CI are evidence rather than authorization.
- Recorded the merged PR #2449 validation and merge evidence.

### Why

Issue #2448 exposed a direct-seed contract regression: `pr_review_context()` had stopped
returning the mutable `pr_diff`, but direct seeding still indexed it and its fixture still
preserved the retired response shape. The correction removed that dependency and kept the
checkout barrier as the only source of review diff text. During PR #2449 review, an initial
API-unreachable audit correctly blocked instead of authorizing; a later live-facts audit
passed, the loop-owned implementation label was read back, and merge-wait merged the exact
reviewed head after required checks passed.

